  "id": "COMPOUND:24902 - PROTEIN:5780",
  "verbalization": "Phyllofolactones F appears to interact with SQ20B through a series of molecular targets, with the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 serving as a common intermediary in multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Phyllofolactones F modulates CD3, which is a key component of the T-cell receptor complex, and that this interaction leads to the activation or inhibition of SQ20B. This mechanism is supported by the presence of a direct target relationship between CD3 and SQ20B in multiple paths, with varying confidence scores indicating a consistent but not absolute link. The presence of two distinct compounds (Caragasinin B and Osugacestat) that target CD3 and ultimately SQ20B further strengthens the hypothesis that Phyllofolactones F exerts its effects via a shared pathway involving CD3. The integration of these findings suggests that Phyllofolactones F may act as a modulator of T-cell signaling, potentially influencing SQ20B through CD3, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
